            <div xml:id="d380">

                <pb facs="0588" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg492"/>

                <head>No. 381.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Schuyler.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 21,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 143.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 175, of the 23d ultimo,
                    covering a printed document relative to the International Statistical Congress
                    to be held at St. Petersburg in August next, has been received. In reply, I have
                    to state that Mr. Edward Young, Chief of the Bureau of Statistics in the
                    Treasury Department, has been appointed a delegate to represent, the United
                    States in said congress.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
